course: dictionary
lesson: 1058
title: Botany: the study of plants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Botany is a science word that tells you what it studies. It means the scientific study of plants: how they grow, what they are made of, how they are named and where they live. A person who does this work is a botanist.
explain: Context gives you clues. «In 1770 Cook landed at Botany Bay and claimed the east coast of Australia for Britain, though Aboriginal people had lived there for over 50,000 years.» The bay has the word botany in its name because plants were studied and collected there. Ask yourself: what would a scientist called a botanist be doing there?
explain: Botany is an uncountable noun, so we do not add a or an to it. You say study botany, not a botany. Other useful phrases are a botanist and a botanical garden.
fact: Botany means the scientific study of plants.
fact: A botanist is a scientist who studies plants.
fact: In science lessons, botany covers parts of a plant, photosynthesis, seeds and pollination.
fact: Botanic gardens show plants from all over the world.
fact: Botany Bay in Australia is named after the plants collected there by Joseph Banks on Captain Cook's voyage.
exercise: «In 1770 Cook landed at Botany Bay.» What does botany mean? | The study of the stars | The study of rocks and fossils | *The scientific study of plants | A type of boat used by sailors
exercise: In science lessons, botany covers photosynthesis, seeds and pollination. Which of these is a topic in botany? | Electricity | Weather fronts | Volcanoes | *How seeds form and spread
exercise: Mia says, "I want to study botany at a botanic garden." Which word means a scientist who studies plants? | Chemist | *Botanist | Explorer | Gardener
test: «Joseph Banks collected plants on Captain Cook's voyage.» Why is Botany Bay named after botany? | *Banks collected and studied plants there | It is a bay full of fishing boats | It was named after a famous ship | It was named by a king's gardener in London
test: Which job would a botanist most likely do? | *Collect and name plants from many places | Count the stars in the sky | Build a bridge over a river | Bake bread for a café
exam: Which definition best matches botany? | The study of old coins and money | *The study of plants: how they grow, what they are made of and where they live | The study of the weather and the seasons | The study of animals and their habits
